                <pb facs="0753" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5034 China—Searchlight Publishing Co./9:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-07-20T16:00:00-04:00">July 20, 1932—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>223. Your 336, July 14, 9 a.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>You should ask Isaacs to
                        call at the Consulate General and inform him (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a</hi>) that his campaign of criticism and vilification of the Chinese
                        Government, which may reasonably be interpreted as an attempt to incite
                        rebellion against that Government, is a gross abuse of his privilege as an
                        American citizen residing in China and is seriously prejudicial to the
                        interests of the United States and its nationals in China; (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">b</hi>) that the Chinese authorities have properly
                        complained of his attacks on the Government of China and have requested the
                        suppression of his offending publication; (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)
                        that he has forfeited any right of protection by the Government of the
                        United States with respect to his publication and, if the present policy of
                        that publication is continued, the registration of the Searchlight
                        Publishing Company as an American enterprise will be cancelled and this
                        Government will not intervene to prevent action by the Chinese authorities
                        against his publication for the purpose of suppressing it.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Inform the Legation.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
